Tom Holland didn't hit the Hollywood  scene so much as he smashed into it at  speed kind of like a meteor with  charisma but for all the sparkle of his  ride to the top there's still a lot we  don't know about the actor here's the  real story behind Marvel's youngest  leading light apparently Tom Holland has  been dancing since he was in diapers in  an interview with The Hollywood Reporter  he recalled that he used to dance to a  Janet Jackson song that his mother would  play when he was a baby this ended up  prompting her to enroll him in a weekly  dance class for children which Holland  took to immediately throwing himself  into everything from ballet to hip-hop  with feverish intensity and although  this was the first step on the road to  becoming one of the world's most famous  actors it was also something schoolyard  bullies were quick to jump on at the  time luckily as he told People magazine  you couldn't hit me hard enough to stop  me from doing it it was this relentless  pursuit of his passion that pushed him  to audition for the titular role in the  West End production of Billy Elliot got  him doing back flips and his audition  tapes for Marvel and ultimately gave him  real-life experience as an underdog  something he now credits as a key  inspiration in his performances Peter  Parker Pollan told People magazine I  like Peter excepted I wasn't the cool  kid at school and just found my group of  friends and got on with it you wouldn't  guess it from the way he seems to revere  every new experience Fame brings him but  Tom isn't the first famous Holland nor  is he the only one who's worked in the  creative arts his father Dominic is a  comedian broadcaster and author while  his mother Nicola  Elizabeth is a photographer despite his  early exposure to the world the  performance and his enrolment in that  weekly dance class Tom's ascent has been  described by his father as a fluke total  fluke what's happened to my son Tom a  real fluke yeah because there's been no  stage school there's been no drama  lessons when Tom's agent proposed  putting together an audition tape for  Marvel the family was roundly skeptical  but now that the impossible has happened  the Holland's credit this unlikely  trajectory is the source of Tom's  down-to-earth nature there are few  superhero costumes quite as iconic as  spider-man's  that's one of the reasons it's barely  changed since its introduction in 1962  from the bold color scheme to the  dramatically flared eyes it was an  instant classic from the moment it  debuted putting on that suit has got to  be pretty daunting for  any newcomer to the role well though  just happen what was that you jumped off  the sign and landed on your face but  it's not just a figurative burden it's  an entirely literal one too in an  interview with shortlist Pollard  revealed that it never occurred to the  crew that he'd need a way to drink in a  suit a problem which demanded a complex  solution a hole is drilled in the eye of  the mask a tube is fed through and an  assistant squeezes water into Holland's  mouth but the consequences of all that  guzzling are just as problematic to  answer nature's call Hollen must strip  down to his regulation underwear which  is nothing more than a thong slap on a  bathrobe and book it to the nearest  bathroom and back as fast as you can  however he's quick to point out that  this hardship is outweighed by the  privilege of getting to bring the iconic  webslinger to life but when you trot off  to see him do his thing in Avengers end  game just remember the spider-man you're  watching probably just took a sip  through the world's most professional  crazy straw everyone knows that Holland  is a pretty goofy guy he's renowned for  his playfulness with Marvel movie  spoilers he's always ready to slap on  some vinyl shorts and perform Rihanna's  Umbrella with the best of them and he  can even find the humor in having to  drink through a straw that someone else  operates for him but it's not all fun  and games  Colin also has some serious ambitions  kid  revenger  he told The Hollywood Reporter the  20-year goal is to be a film director  the 15 year goal is to win an Oscar the  five-year goal is to just keep enjoying  myself he also went on to detail his  acting role models such as Leonardo  DiCaprio Jake Gyllenhaal and Meryl  Streep one thing is clear above all else  Hollen wants to be big he's ready to  work for it and he has a plan as to just  how he's going to accomplish it  Holland didn't expect to ever reach the  peaks of Fame he's already conquered let  alone hit them in his early 20s but it  really can't be emphasized enough that  up until Captain America civil war in  which Holland made his debut as  spider-man he really thought he'd go on  living the life he'd always led  interviews done to promote the  impossible reveal a 16 year old Holland  still certain he's going to go back home  to Kingston and finish up high school  while continuing to pursue his dreams on  the side looking back it's clear that  since Billy Elliott Holland has been on  a speeding train to blockbuster success  after every new production and role he  appears to have thought that things were  going to go back to normal except they  never really did it's only in recent  interviews that Holland seems to have  become someone who truly understands  that his life as he knew it is gone and  that fame is his new normal check out  one of our newest videos right here plus  even more looper videos about your  favorite stop are coming soon subscribe  to our YouTube channel and hit the bell  so you don't miss a single one  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]
 

